Former hockey star Tie Domi is launching a new interview series, " Keeping It Real With Tie ," with Tom Brady as the inaugural guest.

The 12-episode show, which premiered on Nov. 17, will feature conversations with big names in sports, entertainment and business, including Wayne Gretzky, Ray Lewis, Mark Wahlberg, Alex Rodriguez, Cindy Crawford and Mark Messier.

A veteran of 17 NHL seasons, Tahir "Tie" Domi has played on the New York Rangers and Toronto Maple Leafs before retiring in 2006. During his time, he became known as one of the league's toughest players, holding the NHL's all-time record for most career fights with 333. "Keeping It Real With Tie" is designed to shed light on the man behind the reptuation, and Domi expressed wanting the show to be about "connection, shared experiences and the stories that bring people together." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Nicole Kidman to Receive Honorary Cesar From French Film Academy

&#x201C;Where I come from, there&#x2019;s no BS, you show up, you work hard and you take care of your people. That never changes,&#x201D; Domi said in a statement. &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve been lucky to build real friendships with people from all walks of life across sports, entertainment, business and culture. We&#x2019;re sitting down like we always do and talking about what actually got them there, having unscripted, genuine conversations between friends.&#x201D;

"Keeping It Real With Tie" was born out of the time that Domi and his daughter Avery spent together during the pandemic. &#x201C;My dad and I quarantined together during COVID, and when he started sharing stories on Instagram, people loved them," said Avery Domi, an executive producer on the series. "He&#x2019;s always been the best storyteller, and his friends have been telling him for years to do something with it. Bringing this show to life felt like the natural next step, and getting to make it together has been really special." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"Keeping It Real With Tie" will air on DAZN, a sports streaming service, before becoming available on YouTube, Spotify and other podcast platforms.

&#x201C;Keeping It Real with Tie reflects our vision for DAZN Originals — creating compelling content that brings fans closer to the personalities and stories that make sports so special,&#x201D; said Walker Jacobs, global chief revenue officer at DAZN. &#x201C;Tie&#x2019;s relationships extend well beyond hockey, giving us an opportunity to introduce new audiences to the sport while connecting existing fans with some of the biggest names in sports and entertainment. We are excited to be building an original content offering that complements our live sports portfolio and gives fans even more reasons to engage with DAZN.&#x201D;

Since Robert Pattinson was unveiled as James Bond , social media has been awash in jokes about how the seemingly over-employed star &#x2014;&#xA0;who also plays Batman, was recently in "The Odyssey" and is currently on screens in "Primetime" &#x2014;&#xA0;is coming for every job going (yes, even yours).

