In a post on its official account on Wednesday, the government sought to raise awareness of a newly announced youth employment initiative. The scheme is expected to help get more than 90,000 young people across the U.K. into work.

But, taking a slight detour from its usual serious tone, the government chose to highlight the initiative with a picture of Pattinson in his now-iconic Bond reveal photo, alongside the headline: &#x201C;Robert Pattinson to apply for all 90,000 jobs created for young people through youth employment scheme.&#x201D;

The government&#x2019;s trolling of Pattinson is just the latest addition to a growing pile of memes about the star's uncanny ability to keep adding to his already bulging portfolio of roles. Among the lines doing the rounds are: &#x201C;AI won't take my job. Robert Pattinson will,&#x201D; &#x201C;If you have a job right now, that's because Robert Pattinson doesn't want it," and &#x201C;I'm scared to go into the office tomorrow and find Robert Pattinson already sitting at my desk.&#x201D;

As it happens, Pattinson was joking about his appetite for taking other people's jobs long before Bond came his way. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

